---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { news } from '../data/news';
---
<BaseLayout title="Ella Amitay Sadovsky - News" currentPath="news">
  <main>
    <h2 class="page-title">News</h2>

    <section class="prose" style="margin-bottom: 60px; padding-bottom: 40px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">
      <h3 style="font-weight: normal; font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 20px; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase;">Artist Statement</h3>
      <p>My work explores the lived reality of women's lives, as it manifests in both public and domestic spaces, with a particular focus on the gap between utopia and the reality of everyday life. Creating stop-motion video allows me to add a layer of movement to an already multi-layered painting practice.</p>
      <p>My last museum show at the Petach Tikva Museum of Art was the exhibition <em>"Suddenly, Just When You Thought It Was Gone"</em> — a stop-motion video installation based on painting with animated projection layered onto it. The work tells the story of my grandmother, who remained alone on the front line defending her kibbutz against the Arab Legion and the Iraqi army in 1948. Alongside her story are the memories of my father, who was smuggled as a child during the night of the attack to a monastery in Haifa. Also included is my personal story as a child living during the War of Attrition (1967–1970) in an underground shelter, sleeping on foldable iron cots, with almost no exposure to daylight.</p>
      <p>The installation is constructed as a tapestry that presents two worlds, one above the ground and one below, connecting different layers of narrative and time. The space reflects the contrast between subterranean existence and life above ground and water. It moves between past and present, light and darkness, idyllic landscapes and a constant sense of threat and existential struggle.</p>
      <p>The installation <em>Out There</em> (2024), presented at the Wilfrid Israel Museum of Asian Art, consists of three theatrical tableaux. It deals with the Sisyphean nature of female existence, the woman's relationship with her environment, and her journey toward inner freedom, unbound by conventions and prejudices.</p>
      <p>In the project <em>Without Leaving Home</em> (2024), exhibited at Gordon Gallery, I presented a series of paintings that examine the tension between the complex domestic space and the exterior landscape seen through the windows — a view that expresses the possibility of a different gaze, or a dream of escape.</p>
      <p>In my earlier video work <em>Seven</em>, I created a video installation simulating a home inhabited by a person who observes what happens inside and through the windows looking out. The work combines painting and photography and creates a weekly time loop: partners, children, and grandparents enter the home. The installation was awarded the Ann and Ari Rosenblatt Prize for Visual Art (2016).</p>
      <p>My first stop-motion video work, <em>Quiet Island</em> (2012), was a developing painting created on a public bulletin board in Jerusalem, responding to the stories of women who passed by. Around 5,000 paintings were painted one over the other during the course of about six months, forming a collective voice of many women who shared their life stories, desires, and thoughts throughout the project.</p>
    </section>

    {news.map((item) => (
      <article class="news-item" style="display: flex; gap: 30px; margin-bottom: 60px; align-items: flex-start; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 40px;">
        <div class="news-image" style="flex: 0 0 300px;">
          {item.link ? (
            <a href={item.link}>
              <img src={item.image} alt={item.imageAlt} style="width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 4px;" />
            </a>
          ) : (
            <img src={item.image} alt={item.imageAlt} style="width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 4px;" />
          )}
        </div>
        <div class="news-content">
          <span style={`text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: ${item.dateColor ?? '#999'};`}>{item.date}</span>
          <h3 style="margin: 10px 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: normal;">
            {item.link ? (
              <a href={item.link} style="text-decoration: none; color: #222;">{item.title}</a>
            ) : (
              <span style="color: #222;">{item.title}</span>
            )}
          </h3>
          <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #4a90a4; margin-bottom: 10px;">{item.subtitle}</p>
          {item.description && <p style="color: #666; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">{item.description}</p>}
        </div>
      </article>
    ))}
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
